{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00191",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.69,
      "end_seconds": 3.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "Hello doctor, sorry, am I early?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 4.29,
      "end_seconds": 7.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "So, yes, do sit. Tell me what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 9.23,
      "end_seconds": 26.89,
      "duration_seconds": 17.66,
      "text": "Honestly, uh, it's fever and chills, and my family pushed me to come. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest. I told myself I'd wait and see, and here I am."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.7,
      "end_seconds": 29.29,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "And when did that start?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 30.29,
      "end_seconds": 34.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "It's been about two weeks, I'm fairly sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 35.44,
      "end_seconds": 37.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "How bad is it, would you say?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.48,
      "end_seconds": 40.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "I'd say moderate."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 41.53,
      "end_seconds": 44.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "Okay, have you had shortness of breath?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.56,
      "end_seconds": 46.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.3,
      "text": "Yeah, that too."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 48.33,
      "end_seconds": 54.24,
      "duration_seconds": 5.91,
      "text": "What about sharp pain on the right side when you breathe in, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 55.5,
      "end_seconds": 56.47,
      "duration_seconds": 0.97,
      "text": "Yes, actually."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 56.92,
      "end_seconds": 59.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "And coughing up blood, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 60.05,
      "end_seconds": 64.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.37,
      "text": "No, you know, I haven't had any coughing up blood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 65.01,
      "end_seconds": 67.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "Any vomiting, leg swelling or palpitations?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.88,
      "end_seconds": 70.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "No. None of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 70.95,
      "end_seconds": 73.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "Any problems with your joints or muscles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.92,
      "end_seconds": 76.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "No, joints are fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.31,
      "end_seconds": 80.18,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "Any operations in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.65,
      "end_seconds": 85.99,
      "duration_seconds": 4.34,
      "text": "Just my thyroid operated on, a long time ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 87.07,
      "end_seconds": 91.49,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "What about your general health, any conditions you're being treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 91.95,
      "end_seconds": 102.63,
      "duration_seconds": 10.68,
      "text": "I, I have high blood pressure, for two years. I looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.04,
      "end_seconds": 115.03,
      "duration_seconds": 10.99,
      "text": "Right, so that's your known high blood pressure. We'll keep that in mind today. Do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all? These questions might sound routine, but they matter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.17,
      "end_seconds": 119.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "Well, not that I know, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.12,
      "end_seconds": 123.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "Anyone in the family with similar problems or other conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 123.95,
      "end_seconds": 125.89,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "My sister has epilepsy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.4,
      "end_seconds": 127.67,
      "duration_seconds": 1.27,
      "text": "Do you drink alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.19,
      "end_seconds": 131.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "A beer or two most evenings, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.42,
      "end_seconds": 133.4,
      "duration_seconds": 0.98,
      "text": "Do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.47,
      "end_seconds": 137.82,
      "duration_seconds": 1.35,
      "text": "I've never smoked."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.72,
      "end_seconds": 142.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "Is it okay if I type while we talk?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 143.66,
      "end_seconds": 147.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "Yes, um, of course, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.96,
      "end_seconds": 151.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "Any medication at the moment, including things from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.22,
      "end_seconds": 157.86,
      "duration_seconds": 5.64,
      "text": "Okay, so I take ramipril, 5 milligrams, every morning for my blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.17,
      "end_seconds": 161.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "How long have you been on it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.46,
      "end_seconds": 164.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "About a year now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.53,
      "end_seconds": 168.64,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "Let me make a quick note of that before I forget."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 169.38,
      "end_seconds": 170.08,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.63,
      "end_seconds": 182.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. Let me check your vitals now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.16,
      "end_seconds": 195.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.32,
      "text": "Hold still for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 206.06,
      "end_seconds": 212.36,
      "duration_seconds": 6.3,
      "text": "Okay: SpO2 92 percent on room air, pressure 138 over 80, pulse 99. And respiratory rate 24."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 213.72,
      "end_seconds": 217.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "Um, you know, is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.1,
      "end_seconds": 223.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "We'll put it in context in a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.76,
      "end_seconds": 229.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "Alright, I'd like to examine you now. Please come over here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 231.04,
      "end_seconds": 233.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "Turn your head to the side for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.6,
      "end_seconds": 253.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "There's bronchial breathing and crackles at the right lower zone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.0,
      "end_seconds": 261.51,
      "duration_seconds": 5.51,
      "text": "All done, thank you, please sit down. I'll try to keep this as efficient as I can."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 262.45,
      "end_seconds": 265.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "Thank you, I appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.95,
      "end_seconds": 280.24,
      "duration_seconds": 14.29,
      "text": "So, based on the history and the examination, it fits best with a possible pneumonia on the right side. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more. I'd also keep a pulmonary embolism in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 280.99,
      "end_seconds": 285.1,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "Right, um, is it something serious, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 286.42,
      "end_seconds": 302.09,
      "duration_seconds": 15.67,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now a possible pneumonia on the right side is my leading thought, not anything worse. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had fever and chills for about two weeks, moderate, and no vomiting or leg swelling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 303.56,
      "end_seconds": 305.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "That's it, uh, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 309.22,
      "end_seconds": 339.31,
      "duration_seconds": 30.09,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange blood tests for infection. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step. Let's use amoxicillin-clavulanate, 625 milligrams, three times a day, for five days. That should help with chest infection. I'll put all of this in writing so you don't have to remember it. Rest and fluids, and finish every dose of the antibiotic. A short walk every day, even twenty minutes, will help more than you'd think."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 340.82,
      "end_seconds": 354.1,
      "duration_seconds": 13.28,
      "text": "Avoid taking any extra painkillers on top of what I'm prescribing without checking with us. Please don't sit on it if the breathlessness worsens or you become drowsy. That's the point to get seen urgently."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 359.05,
      "end_seconds": 361.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Got it, you know, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 362.85,
      "end_seconds": 364.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "Come back after the X-ray."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 368.86,
      "end_seconds": 371.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "Okay, you know, I'll book that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 372.36,
      "end_seconds": 378.62,
      "duration_seconds": 6.26,
      "text": "Just so I know I've explained it clearly, can you tell me the plan back in your own words?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 379.97,
      "end_seconds": 389.07,
      "duration_seconds": 9.1,
      "text": "So, I take the amoxicillin-clavulanate, 625 milligrams, three times a day and come back after the X-ray. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 391.58,
      "end_seconds": 396.13,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Good. Call the clinic if you need us in the meantime."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 397.03,
      "end_seconds": 399.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Well, no questions. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 401.02,
      "end_seconds": 402.12,
      "duration_seconds": 1.1,
      "text": "See you then."
    }
  ]
}